[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SharpUnits remaining Java unit grammar requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: JP-014-POWERS
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Java textual power forms
STATEMENT: The Java quantity parser shall support bounded ASCII, double-star and superscript 1/2/3 power notation using pinned SimpleUnitFormat semantics, including the zero-literal sentinel, without changing native unit power APIs.
COMMENT: Implementation: JavaUnitTextParser.cs. Verification: ParserGrammarTests and shared H100 scenarios. Evidence: conformance/parser-grammar-review-100.json. Exponent magnitude remains bounded by 1024.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: JP-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: JP-014-ROOTS
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rational textual powers and roots
STATEMENT: The Java quantity parser shall preserve rational dimensions for bounded colon-root exponents, with Java power-then-root scale evaluation and documented floating-point limits.
COMMENT: Implementation: JavaUnitTextParser.cs. Verification: ParserGrammarTests and shared H100 scenarios. Evidence: conformance/parser-grammar-review-100.json. Affine algebra and nonfinite numeric factors remain rejected.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: JP-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: JP-014-INTEGER-FACTOR
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Integer factors in unit expressions
STATEMENT: The Java quantity parser shall support nonzero signed 32-bit integer factors after multiplication/division, preserving pinned operator association and scale.
COMMENT: Implementation: JavaUnitTextParser.cs, UnitDefinition and JavaDoubleArithmetic. Verification: ParserGrammarTests and shared H100 scenarios, including conversion through nonterminating factors 1/3 and 1/7. Exact internal linear factors use a 16384-bit allocation budget. Evidence: conformance/parser-grammar-review-100.json. Fractional numeric factors and Java integer-overflow quirks outside this range remain explicit gaps.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: JP-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: JP-014-PREFIXES
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Automatic decimal-prefix resolution
STATEMENT: The Java quantity parser shall resolve supported single decimal prefixes on registered coherent linear units without registry mutation, with exact registrations taking precedence.
COMMENT: Implementation: JavaUnitTextParser.cs and SiPrefixes.cs. Verification: ParserGrammarTests and shared H100 scenarios. Evidence: conformance/parser-grammar-review-100.json. The Greek micro alias is normalized. Nested/affine prefixes and general Java unit discovery are not implied.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: JP-014
